  "id": "Compound::DB00575 - Gene::152",
  "verbalization": "Clonidine, through its inclusion in the Adrenergic Alpha2-agonists class, binds to Adra1b, which is involved in Alpha-adrenergic receptor activity. This activity is then participated by Adra2c, suggesting a potential role in the regulation of Adra2c function. Additionally, Clonidine is linked to Adra2c through the binding of Clonidine to Adra1b, which is part of a broader network of interactions involving Alpha-adrenergic receptors. The evidence suggests that Clonidine may influence Adra2c through its interaction with Adra1b, which in turn modulates the activity of Adra2c. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Clonidine exerts its effects on Adra2c, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
